-- title:
--   Maximal ideal at a crossing: p and the chart coordinates
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` for $M/p \mid M$ is trivial, and the hypothesis `hj` that the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field of level $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for $X_H(M)$ over the base ring `R p`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R p \to A$ compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a map $\rho_O : R p \to O$, maximal ideal generated by $p$, equipped with a surjection $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa(A)$ lifting the residue map of $\rho$, a map $j_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with $\rho_O$, and a map $\iota_A : O \to A$ inducing $j_O$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa$. Write $X_O$ for `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, the base change of the model to $O$, and for $i \in \{0,1\}$ let $c_i$ be the composite of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho\,i$ with the base-change morphism `bcMap` from the special fibre over $\kappa(A)$ to $X_O$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho\,0$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho\,1$, and let $x_n \in X_O$ be the image of $n$ under the first projection followed by $c_0$. Let $e \ge 1$, let $U$ be an open subscheme of $X_O$ containing $x_n$, and let $f : U \to \mathrm{Spec}\,O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - p^e)$ be a morphism over $\mathrm{Spec}\,O$, in the sense that $f$ followed by the structure morphism of the crossing algebra equals the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow X_O$ followed by the projection $X_O \to \mathrm{Spec}\,O$. Assume: a point $y$ of $U$ has both `CrossingQuotient.U` and `CrossingQuotient.V` in the prime $f(y)$ exactly when $y$ lies over $x_n$; at every $y$ over $x_n$ the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal and induces an isomorphism of residue fields, and $y$ has an open neighbourhood $V$ in $U$ with $V \hookrightarrow U \to \mathrm{Spec}\,O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-p^e)$ étale; and, for every $y$, membership of `CrossingQuotient.V` in $f(y)$ is equivalent to $y$ lying in the image of $c_0$, while membership of `CrossingQuotient.U` in $f(y)$ is equivalent to $y$ lying in the image of $c_1$. Finally let $x$ be a point of $X_O$ lying in the open image of $U$ with $x = x_n$. Then the maximal ideal of the stalk of $X_O$ at $x$ is generated by the three germs at $x$, over that open image, of the sections obtained by pulling back along $f$ the three elements $p$, `CrossingQuotient.U (p^e)` and `CrossingQuotient.V (p^e)` of $O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-p^e)$.
--
--   This is the local algebra at a crossing point of the two components of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ after base change to $O$: an étale chart of the form $X_0X_1 = p^e$ exhibits the maximal ideal of the local ring as generated by $p$ together with the two chart coordinates. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.ord_placeOn_germ_chart_eq_one_of_chart_of_residue_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.ord_placeOn_germ_chart_eq_one_of_chart_of_residue_surjective), which computes the order of vanishing of a chart coordinate germ along a component.
